In JavaScript, you can use the `getElementsByTagName` method to get a collection of elements, and then use the `focus()` method to focus on a specific element in that collection.

Here's an example:
```javascript
// Get the collection of elements
var elements = document.getElementsByTagName('input');

// Focus on the first element in the collection
elements[0].focus();
```
This will focus on the first `<input>` element found in the document.

If you want to focus on a specific element by its name or id, you can use `getElementsByName` or `getElementById` instead:
```javascript
// Focus on an element by name
var element = document.getElementsByName('myInput')[0];
element.focus();

// Focus on an element by id
var element = document.getElementById('myInput');
element.focus();
```
